deep.reconstruction:
Setting (from the previous pages): X is a topological space, I is an ordered set, and i ↦ X_i is an increasing family of closed subsets of X. The previous page defined two spaces:
- X_{Δ0} = {(x,i) ∈ X×I : x ∈ X_i}, which is the disjoint union ∐_i X_i;
- X_{Δ1} ⊂ X_{Δ0}×X_{Δ0}, the graph of the order (x,i) ≤ (y,j) ⟺ x = y and i ≤ j.
The pair (X_{Δ0}, X_{Δ1}) is thus an internal poset, hence an internal category, in Top. Composition (9) is X_{Δ2} := X_{Δ1} ×_{X_{Δ0}} X_{Δ1} → X_{Δ1}.

This page writes out the r-fold fibre products, which are the levels of the nerve. In (10):
- X_{Δr} = {(x_0 ≤ … ≤ x_r)} ⊂ X_{Δ0}^{r+1};
- equivalently, X_{Δr} ≅ {(x, i_0 ≤ … ≤ i_r) : x ∈ X_{i_0}} ⊂ X×I^{r+1};
- equivalently, X_{Δr} ≅ ∐_{i_* ∈ I(Δr)} X_{i_0};
- equivalently, X_{Δr} ≅ ∐_{i_0} X_{i_0} × (flags of length r−1 in I_{≥ i_0}).
Here I(Δr) = Hom_ord(Δr, I) is the set of (possibly degenerate) flags of length r, i.e. the r-simplices of the nerve N(I). The identification is legitimate because x ∈ X_{i_0} ⊂ X_{i_k} for every k, since the family is increasing.

By the 'well-known' nerve construction, the X_{Δr} form a simplicial space X_{Δ*}. (Grothendieck writes '½ simplicial', which is the old 'semi-simplicial' meaning simplicial, since all increasing α are allowed, so degeneracies are included.) Functoriality is given by α*(x, i_*) = (x, i_*∘α), i.e. X_{Δ*} ⊂ X × N(I) as a simplicial subspace (next page).

In modern terms, X_{Δ*} is the nerve of the topological Grothendieck construction of the diagram i ↦ X_i. Equivalently it is the simplicial replacement (Bousfield–Kan) of the functor I → Top whose geometric realization is hocolim_I X_i. It comes with projections to X (constant simplicial space) and to N(I). The fibre over x is the nerve of the up-closed subposet I_x = {i : x ∈ X_i}.

Purpose: in the 'topos stratifié' context, this provides a simplicial (Mayer–Vietoris / Čech-type) resolution of a space equipped with a poset-indexed closed filtration or stratification. It is used to compare X, or its topos, with the descent data over the closed pieces.
